<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	20.43	    +113	    20.03     21.00</p>
<p>91-Day	21.78	    +47	     21.64     21.88</p>
<p>182-Day     22.03	    +4		21.89     22.15</p>
<p>357-Day     22.96				22.90     23.00</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 22.92 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.34 bln pesos     2.93</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   4.16 bln pesos     5.2</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   3.94 bln pesos     4.91</p>
<p>357-Day     600 million pesos   3.17 bln pesos     5.28</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.53 on demand of 13.6 billion pesos compared with 3.52 the week before, on demand of 10.55 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   57 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   10 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  12 basis points</p>
<p>    357-Day			   4 basis points</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
